00:18:23.538 --> 00:18:25.006
And anything you find
without a warrant


00:18:25.038 --> 00:18:27.509
is fruit of the poison tree.


00:18:28.675 --> 00:18:30.244
I'm sorry, sis.


00:18:30.278 --> 00:18:32.246
Okay, we're legal.


00:18:32.278 --> 00:18:34.382
- Over there.
- All right!


00:18:34.414 --> 00:18:37.284
Susie, Cash, how y'all doin'?


00:18:40.721 --> 00:18:42.089
Move.


00:18:42.123 --> 00:18:43.923
Randy, want to start
at the bathroom?


00:18:43.958 --> 00:18:45.026
Sure.


00:18:45.058 --> 00:18:46.426
- You all right?
- Yeah.


00:18:46.460 --> 00:18:48.062
Why don't you go sit down
there, around the coffee table.


00:18:48.095 --> 00:18:49.264
I told you not
to let anyone in


00:18:49.297 --> 00:18:50.464
unless they showed
you a warrant.


00:18:50.530 --> 00:18:52.198
He showed me his
gun, all right?


00:18:52.232 --> 00:18:53.466
I didn't mean
that as a question.


00:18:53.468 --> 00:18:54.769
I said sit down.


00:19:02.143 --> 00:19:04.578
Ain't you got
somethin' to say?


00:19:05.380 --> 00:19:06.280
I didn't start this.


00:19:06.314 --> 00:19:08.480
You can stop it though.


00:19:08.482 --> 00:19:11.484
You want me to save
your dumb brother's ass?


00:19:11.486 --> 00:19:12.620
It's none of my business,
but I'd be worried


00:19:12.653 --> 00:19:14.756
about saving my own
ass right now, Cash.


00:19:14.788 --> 00:19:16.156
Is that right?


00:19:16.223 --> 00:19:17.823
Well, the cocaine
residue on the table alone


00:19:17.825 --> 00:19:19.059
is enough to violate you,


00:19:19.094 --> 00:19:20.826
send you back to
prison for two years.


00:19:20.828 --> 00:19:22.995
That is if your wife
flushed your whole stash,


00:19:22.997 --> 00:19:24.230
which I somehow doubt.


00:19:24.265 --> 00:19:27.134
Been peepin' through
keyholes, have you?


00:19:27.167 --> 00:19:29.069
Absolutely.


00:19:29.104 --> 00:19:31.239
Got a mirror in here.


00:19:32.574 --> 00:19:35.677
Looks like it was
used in a bakery.


00:19:38.645 --> 00:19:41.816
And a big ol' bag of
hillbilly heroin.


00:19:42.650 --> 00:19:44.686
Those are prescription!


00:19:46.186 --> 00:19:50.524
You got a prescription
for a thousands Percocet?


00:19:55.363 --> 00:19:57.298
He's got somethin' worth
a lot more than that.


00:19:58.532 --> 00:19:59.866
He knows somethin' that
will get him a deal


00:19:59.933 --> 00:20:01.269
and Bones one too.


00:20:02.536 --> 00:20:06.371
I don't want to be a party
to nobody gettin' ratted out!


00:20:06.373 --> 00:20:08.543
Be quiet, now, honey.


00:20:14.048 --> 00:20:16.283
What's that, Cash?


00:20:16.317 --> 00:20:18.152
I said I ain't sayin' nothin'


00:20:18.185 --> 00:20:20.553
until I get a deal in writin'.


00:20:20.621 --> 00:20:22.721
Oh, you've done
this before, huh?


00:20:22.723 --> 00:20:25.460
He's dones this
lots of times before.


00:20:25.492 --> 00:20:26.994
What do you say
we leave Cash here


00:20:27.028 --> 00:20:28.328
to think over his
limited options


00:20:28.362 --> 00:20:30.228
and take the brother
for drugs for now.


00:20:30.230 --> 00:20:32.799
I say we can do
whatever we want.


00:20:32.834 --> 00:20:34.168
All right.


00:20:34.201 --> 00:20:35.901
Bones shot that
boy in self-defense!


00:20:35.903 --> 00:20:37.401
That's a fact!


00:20:37.403 --> 00:20:38.806
Randy, man, listen for a second.


00:20:38.839 --> 00:20:39.807
Get off me!


00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:40.907
I'd say you're
on stronger ground


00:20:40.909 --> 00:20:43.075
that trying to talk your
husband into making a deal.


00:20:43.077 --> 00:20:44.412
Oh, is that right?


00:20:44.478 --> 00:20:46.413
Yeah, that's right.


00:20:48.481 --> 00:20:50.350
You hear that, Dick Four?


00:20:50.384 --> 00:20:55.490
I know where we're gettin'
outta this is if we make a deal.


00:20:58.259 --> 00:21:00.326
I gotta small wife, too, Cash.


00:21:00.361 --> 00:21:03.598
I find it best to
shut up and listen.


00:21:04.332 --> 00:21:05.533
Night-night.


00:21:09.569 --> 00:21:11.538
Okay, let me get this straight.


00:21:11.573 --> 00:21:13.374
You want a weekly salary.


00:21:13.407 --> 00:21:14.741
You want to be off probation,


00:21:14.775 --> 00:21:16.544
want to negotiate the
size of your bonus


00:21:16.577 --> 00:21:18.779
for this information before
you tell us what it is,


00:21:18.846 --> 00:21:22.849
and if you testify, you want
to be in witness protection?


00:21:22.883 --> 00:21:24.115
That's it?


00:21:24.117 --> 00:21:25.886
Mm-Hm.


00:21:25.920 --> 00:21:29.757
You do realise that's
a lot to ask, right?


00:21:29.790 --> 00:21:32.393
And even if you're John
Gotti, that's a lot to ask.


00:21:32.426 --> 00:21:35.929
Well, I got to a lot to offer.


00:21:35.962 --> 00:21:37.464
Who's John Gotti?


00:21:43.136 --> 00:21:44.538
All right.


00:21:44.571 --> 00:21:47.106
Entertain our guests
while I speak to my boss?


00:21:47.141 --> 00:21:48.043
Yeah.


00:21:48.977 --> 00:21:51.980
I'll tell 'em my fishin' story.


00:21:52.046 --> 00:21:55.048
So me an my cousin Fred, we
was out noodlin' one day...


00:21:55.083 --> 00:21:56.284
Eh, you got a phone I can use?


00:21:56.317 --> 00:21:58.817
Big guy, 'cause
he's from my mom's side.


00:21:58.819 --> 00:21:59.820
In private.


00:22:02.923 --> 00:22:05.460
Grabs it by lower lip,
pulls it outta the hole,


00:22:05.492 --> 00:22:08.661
wraps his legs
around the tail...


00:22:11.231 --> 00:22:12.800
62-pound flathead.


00:22:14.999 --> 00:22:15.102
He reached in with his hand?


00:22:15.135 --> 00:22:16.503
Yeah.


00:22:16.570 --> 00:22:17.404
They was noodlin',
you moron...


00:22:18.772 --> 00:22:19.440
Creekview.


00:22:19.473 --> 00:22:20.506
Who asked you?


00:22:20.574 --> 00:22:22.308
Susan Smith?


00:22:22.343 --> 00:22:23.342
Yeah?


00:22:23.344 --> 00:22:25.013
Y'all got a call.


00:22:39.859 --> 00:22:40.861
Yeah?


00:22:41.929 --> 00:22:43.798
It's me, your sister.


00:22:44.765 --> 00:22:46.801
- Somethin' wrong with the kids?
- No, no.


00:22:46.835 --> 00:22:50.604
Just someone from the Welfare
in West Virginia called.


00:22:50.637 --> 00:22:52.005
Shit.


00:22:52.039 --> 00:22:53.641
She was checkin' up on you.


00:22:53.673 --> 00:22:55.776
You're sure
she's from Welfare?


00:22:55.809 --> 00:22:59.047
Yeah, she knew your
case numbers and everything.


00:22:59.113 --> 00:23:00.847
All right, anything else?


00:23:00.881 --> 00:23:02.216
No, I just...


00:23:02.282 --> 00:23:04.382
thought you'd wanna know.


00:23:04.384 --> 00:23:05.383
Yeah, all right.


00:23:05.385 --> 00:23:06.788
Thanks.


00:23:06.820 --> 00:23:07.855
See ya later.


00:23:12.059 --> 00:23:15.395
Meet me in the parking lot
of the drive-thru at 7:00 a.m.


00:23:15.462 --> 00:23:16.394
7:00 a.m.?


00:23:16.396 --> 00:23:18.398
Why would I do that?


00:23:18.465 --> 00:23:20.466
To get your brother
a better deal.


00:23:20.500 --> 00:23:22.567
Keep your husband out of prison.


00:23:22.569 --> 00:23:26.206
Maybe get a little
somethin' for yourself, too.


00:23:26.240 --> 00:23:27.540
I don't want to talk
to Cash anymore.


00:23:27.575 --> 00:23:30.044
I wanna talk to the boss.


00:23:30.077 --> 00:23:31.479
When he asks you what
the call was about,


00:23:31.512 --> 00:23:33.580
say, "None of your
business, you don't own me."


00:23:33.647 --> 00:23:36.583
That way I'll know
you're comin'.


00:23:38.086 --> 00:23:40.755
You sicked the Welfare on me.


00:23:43.490 --> 00:23:44.592
There another option?


00:23:45.826 --> 00:23:48.261
Maybe ask for
something reasonable.


00:23:48.328 --> 00:23:50.664
His goddam boss said no.


00:23:53.500 --> 00:23:56.436
I did say you were
asking for too much, Cash.


00:23:56.503 --> 00:23:57.938
Well, if you want
to catch big fish,


00:23:58.005 --> 00:23:59.939
you gotta cut good bait.


00:23:59.941 --> 00:24:02.242
Did you really
tell them a fishing story?


00:24:02.276 --> 00:24:03.443
Yeah, I did.


00:24:03.510 --> 00:24:06.079
I didn't think it would
affect his mind, though.


00:24:06.113 --> 00:24:07.047
That's not funny, man.


00:24:07.080 --> 00:24:09.783
I got a lot to think about here.


00:24:11.785 --> 00:24:14.452
Who was bothering you
back there, anyway?


00:24:14.454 --> 00:24:16.691
None of your business.


00:24:19.093 --> 00:24:20.628
You don't own me.


00:24:26.634 --> 00:24:27.902
We done here?


00:24:29.569 --> 00:24:32.639
I could do with
a cup of coffee.


00:24:34.208 --> 00:24:35.210
Waitress!


00:25:10.176 --> 00:25:11.844
God damn her.


00:25:31.598 --> 00:25:32.299
There.


00:25:32.432 --> 00:25:35.502
This is for coming
to meet me today.


00:25:51.518 --> 00:25:52.720
Nice ride.


00:25:53.554 --> 00:25:54.788
Yeah?


00:25:56.156 --> 00:25:57.958
I inherited it from the
guy I replaced here.


00:25:57.991 --> 00:26:00.461
He just left for his new
assignment in Los Angeles.


00:26:00.494 --> 00:26:01.695
Lucky him.


00:26:02.896 --> 00:26:05.298
You're not a big
fan of Pikeville?


00:26:05.332 --> 00:26:06.801
I grew up in a town
about this size.


00:26:06.834 --> 00:26:09.336
Alls I know is every
time I fall down,


00:26:09.369 --> 00:26:10.903
I end up Rollin'
right back here.


00:26:10.971 --> 00:26:15.142
I figure that makes this
the bottom of the world.


00:26:15.175 --> 00:26:17.511
Well, your husband's
negotiated himself out of a deal


00:26:17.545 --> 00:26:20.247
that could get you
both outta here.


00:26:20.314 --> 00:26:22.816
Is he always this hard-headed
about getting what he wants?


00:26:22.849 --> 00:26:25.485
He won my heart, didn't he?


00:26:25.519 --> 00:26:27.920
And you keep callin'
him my husband.


00:26:27.922 --> 00:26:28.923
He's my ex.


00:26:29.890 --> 00:26:32.226
Yeah, but you live together.


00:26:32.259 --> 00:26:35.362
We live under the same roof.


00:26:35.395 --> 00:26:36.931
But we're not together.


00:26:38.164 --> 00:26:40.701
I can see he's not
smart enough for you.


00:26:40.733 --> 00:26:42.433
He's a dick four.


00:26:42.435 --> 00:26:44.070
What is a dick four, anyway?


00:26:49.042 --> 00:26:50.110
Well now.


00:26:50.178 --> 00:26:52.680
I just gotta keep that in
my little book of memories,


00:26:52.712 --> 00:26:54.615
mister hot shot FBI.


00:26:55.782 --> 00:26:59.853
I guess a shoulda seen
that one coming, huh?


00:27:02.789 --> 00:27:06.027
So what to you want
most outta life, Susan?


00:27:06.059 --> 00:27:07.594
Seriously, what would
turn your life around


00:27:07.627 --> 00:27:10.464
right now if it happened?


00:27:10.530 --> 00:27:11.398
You must think about it.


00:27:11.432 --> 00:27:12.799
I certainly do.


00:27:16.971 --> 00:27:17.971
Rehab.


00:27:21.308 --> 00:27:22.309
And money.


00:27:26.079 --> 00:27:27.314
Rehab and money.


00:27:34.954 --> 00:27:37.290
So you're a drug addict
who wants to get help,


00:27:37.325 --> 00:27:41.492
but you live with your
ex who's a coke dealer.


00:27:41.494 --> 00:27:43.663
I imagine that must be hard.


00:27:43.730 --> 00:27:44.899
I didn't say any of that.


00:27:44.932 --> 00:27:45.932
You did.


00:27:47.834 --> 00:27:51.405
Why don't I tell you
what I really want.


00:27:52.673 --> 00:27:54.808
I know what you want.


00:27:56.343 --> 00:28:00.815
And I know what's a federal
crime and what ain't.


00:28:04.852 --> 00:28:08.823
That's the
way the devil comes.


00:28:13.527 --> 00:28:16.029
He don't come to you as evil.


00:28:21.601 --> 00:28:24.138
He don't come to you on fire.


00:28:28.875 --> 00:28:32.279
He comes as everything
you ever wanted.


00:28:36.383 --> 00:28:39.120
He comes to you as you.


00:28:41.654 --> 00:28:44.722
That's my pappy right there.


00:28:44.724 --> 00:28:45.492
Hiram Grembly.


00:28:46.826 --> 00:28:51.732
And on the other side is
Cash's daddy, Amos G. Smith.


00:28:52.232 --> 00:28:53.834
Son of a bitch.


00:28:53.866 --> 00:28:55.368
So I remember you
saying when you fall down


00:28:55.402 --> 00:28:56.567
you always end up back here.


00:28:56.569 --> 00:28:57.736
Where did you fall down?


00:28:57.738 --> 00:29:00.238
You remember
everything I say, do you?


00:29:00.240 --> 00:29:01.875
Yeah, of course.


00:29:04.479 --> 00:29:05.744
Pittsburgh.


00:29:05.746 --> 00:29:09.016
Me and Cash, we lived in
Pittsburgh for a year.


00:29:09.048 --> 00:29:10.817
Why don't you tell me about
some of Cash's customers?


00:29:12.086 --> 00:29:15.389
You know, what they do for a
living, that kind of stuff.


00:29:15.422 --> 00:29:18.025
You mean what other
crimes do they commit


00:29:18.057 --> 00:29:20.361
that you can get
'em jammed up for?


00:29:20.394 --> 00:29:21.394
Exactly.


00:29:24.832 --> 00:29:28.736
Mark, I'd be takin'
a hell of a big risk.


00:29:28.769 --> 00:29:31.038
These people don't fuck around.


00:29:31.070 --> 00:29:33.673
They find out you're a snitch,
they burn down your house,


00:29:33.707 --> 00:29:36.343
and that is just a warnin'.


00:29:36.376 --> 00:29:38.011
You keep doin' it, they
will cut out your tongue


00:29:38.045 --> 00:29:39.446
and feed it to their dogs.


00:29:39.512 --> 00:29:42.750
That's why they'd be willing
to put you through rehab,


00:29:42.784 --> 00:29:45.186
send you and your kids
to a new state somewhere,


00:29:45.219 --> 00:29:48.556
give you a new
identity, a decent job.


00:29:49.923 --> 00:29:51.223
They do that?


00:29:51.258 --> 00:29:52.457
Yeah.


00:29:52.459 --> 00:29:54.128
They do it all the time.


00:29:55.262 --> 00:29:58.698
Look, if you help me bring
down this bank robber,


00:29:58.731 --> 00:30:01.535
I bet they pay you 10 grand.


00:30:01.567 --> 00:30:02.970
Yeah, 10 grand.


00:30:04.471 --> 00:30:06.306
I'm not judging you, Susan.


00:30:06.373 --> 00:30:07.774
I'm just saying, you've
never tried to make


00:30:07.807 --> 00:30:09.544
a clean break of it,
so don't give up hope.


00:30:09.576 --> 00:30:11.476
It's hope that's
fuckin' me up.


00:30:11.478 --> 00:30:13.113
I understand.


00:30:13.145 --> 00:30:14.480
Here.


00:30:14.548 --> 00:30:15.782
Take this for now.


00:30:15.816 --> 00:30:18.552
Just remember, big
risks pay big money.


00:30:18.586 --> 00:30:20.822
Small risks, small money.


00:30:22.088 --> 00:30:23.089
Okay?


00:32:16.769 --> 00:32:18.605
Pretty, ain't they?


00:32:21.240 --> 00:32:24.177
You wanna hold one of them guns?


00:32:24.944 --> 00:32:26.579
They feel like...


00:32:28.281 --> 00:32:29.282
power.


00:32:29.950 --> 00:32:31.184
You know?


00:32:39.460 --> 00:32:44.597
Just make sure you read the
papers the next few days, okay?


00:32:47.768 --> 00:32:50.471
Easy Street's just down yonder.


00:33:04.384 --> 00:33:05.218
Come on!


00:33:09.823 --> 00:33:10.758
Damn.


00:33:12.092 --> 00:33:14.659
You ain't started goin'
to church again, have you?


00:33:14.661 --> 00:33:16.163
Why?


00:33:16.230 --> 00:33:18.298
You wouldn't care if
I was being ordained.


00:33:18.332 --> 00:33:19.333
Am I right?


00:33:28.608 --> 00:33:29.275
Come on, Susan!


00:33:29.309 --> 00:33:30.743
You can't keep doing this to me.


00:33:30.778 --> 00:33:31.944
If you want me to
keep paying you,


00:33:31.979 --> 00:33:33.413
you have to give me something.


00:33:33.446 --> 00:33:34.247
Seriously.


00:33:34.280 --> 00:33:35.513
I've given you
hundreds of dollars,


00:33:35.515 --> 00:33:37.251
and you haven't given
me a goddam thing.


00:33:37.284 --> 00:33:38.951
I keep telling you.


00:33:38.984 --> 00:33:40.987
My life would be in danger.


00:33:41.021 --> 00:33:43.923
I know, but your life's
in danger now, isn't it?


00:33:47.627 --> 00:33:50.496
How long you think
you can keep this up?


00:33:50.530 --> 00:33:54.934
How long before you find
yourself in jail or dead?


00:33:54.968 --> 00:33:56.003
Then what are your
kids gonna do?


00:33:56.036 --> 00:33:57.201
How are they gonna live?


00:33:57.203 --> 00:33:58.370
You think the judge
will give 'em the cash,


00:33:58.438 --> 00:33:59.874
or you think they'll
wind up in foster care?


00:33:59.940 --> 00:34:00.774
You got a kid, huh?


00:34:00.807 --> 00:34:02.342
Yeah.


00:34:02.375 --> 00:34:03.309
Wife too?


00:34:04.144 --> 00:34:06.211
We're talkin'
about you, Susan.


00:34:06.278 --> 00:34:08.615
Tell me what she's like.


00:34:13.853 --> 00:34:15.056
Is she young?


00:34:17.891 --> 00:34:19.225
Is she pretty?


00:34:20.793 --> 00:34:23.129
Does she have a good body?


00:34:25.065 --> 00:34:29.066
She keeps herself fit,
if that's what you mean.


00:34:29.068 --> 00:34:31.735
Oh, she's too
high-class for me.


00:34:31.737 --> 00:34:32.405
Is that it?


00:34:32.472 --> 00:34:33.574
No.


00:34:33.639 --> 00:34:37.643
'Cause high class ain't a
always so good in a woman.


00:34:37.677 --> 00:34:39.378
If she won't suck your
dick at the movies,


00:34:39.413 --> 00:34:40.744
then what the hell
kinda good is she?


00:34:40.746 --> 00:34:42.649
Oh, come on.
Stop it.


00:34:43.918 --> 00:34:45.251
Cash may treat you
like a cheap whore,


00:34:45.318 --> 00:34:47.853
but that's no reason
to talk like one.


00:34:47.887 --> 00:34:48.856
Susan.


00:34:50.490 --> 00:34:52.590
You're the key to
everything I wanna do here.


00:34:52.592 --> 00:34:54.592
Do you understand that?


00:34:54.594 --> 00:34:57.530
To me, you're the most
important woman in this town.


00:34:57.563 --> 00:35:00.701
For God sake, learn
to act like it.


00:36:00.960 --> 00:36:02.827
He's name's Joe-Bea.


00:36:02.829 --> 00:36:04.832
My ex met him in prison.


00:36:05.831 --> 00:36:07.400
He lives with us.


00:36:09.168 --> 00:36:11.103
He has for four months.


00:36:11.137 --> 00:36:13.838
I didn't know how to tell you.


00:36:13.840 --> 00:36:14.842
I'm sorry.


00:36:20.514 --> 00:36:21.682
Outstanding.


00:36:24.117 --> 00:36:26.952
You've actually
seen the shotguns?


